{quote}I am feeling a little deviation form the designs still{quote}

We are using system iOS date picker component where design slightly differs for each version. Here I’ve posted the board comparing all major versions and seems like everyone is OK with the default appearance

[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02GQ6KNK63/p1660920322972769?thread_ts=1660745711.458719&cid=C02GQ6KNK63|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02GQ6KNK63/p1660920322972769?thread_ts=1660745711.458719&cid=C02GQ6KNK63|smart-link] 

{quote}Also, the keyboard doesn’t seem to appear while on sim but I could edit the time using my keyboard.{quote}

It is because by default iOS simulator uses hardware keyboard for the input. You still could use Testflight to download nightly builds to check this functionality, because this is better to check on real devices indeed.

{quote}Also, I could schedule a ride after the time passed and it didn’t repotted to the nearest next time

But when I try to change/edit the time picker is updated{quote}

Yes, this is how it currently works. On client side we do not update closest possible pickup time when you are staying on the screen. The check is done only on next pickup opening or on ride creation. For your case if you’ve tapped “schedule ride” with invalid time BE is supposed to throw an error and mobile should display an alert explaining the reasoning with proposal to open picker again. That’s an expected behaviour I guess.

