Internal signing delegation is explained in this [Policy.|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BILP/pages/1525121359/Contract+Review+Signatory+Authority+Policy] You would need the PoA if the Policy does not give you the authorisation to sign or if the Policy authorises you to sign, but the external party requests a proof of you signing rights (i.e. PoA).

If the Policy does not give you the authorisation to sign, then the issuance of the PoA for you needs to be approved by the approver (see from the Policy). Please include the approver to the ticket, it will be sufficient if the approver approves the issuance of the PoA for you under this ticket.

Following info is required to draft the PoA:

* Your full legal name;
* Your personal identification code and country of its issuer;
* Indication of which Bolt entity you need signing rights on behalf of;
* Indication of which Oyster company (details of the legal entity: name, registry code, address) the PoA is needed for;
* Whether a digital PoA with e-signature is sufficient or if you require a hard copy signed with wet ink to be mailed to you
* Specific details of what rights need to be included? Please be clear and specific as possible. PoA’s will only be approved with narrow rights to fit your needs.
* If you have, can you also please send me the copy of the previous PoA with Oyster?

Thank you\!

