As discussed here is the tentative API spec:

Input:

{noformat}[
    {
        id: string, // just an identifier to easily get back
                    // the matching campaigns from the output
        country: string,
        cityId: number,
        providerTraits: string[]
    },
    ...
]{noformat}

Output (only approved campaigns):

{noformat}[
    {
        id: string, // the matching id from input
        campaigns:
        [
            {
                id: number, // Campaign ID
                start: number, // Unix timestamp
                end: number, // Unix timestamp
                menu_item_tags: string[],
                bonus_data: BonusData
            }
        ] 
    }
]{noformat}

Feel free to adjust it; especially the output, since you're more familiar with the conventions for the Campaign fields.

Note that the alternative to having the {{id: string}} in the input (and output) is to have an output array that matches the input array size (and we would be able to match each input element in the output using the array index).

{quote}I guess since you are passing an array of provider traits, you are expecting campaigns that have any of those traits, right?{quote}

Yes, exactly. So one element from the input may match multiple campaigns.

{quote}So, you would need to know for each campaign that we return which trait was actually matched.{quote}

We don’t actually need this information. It’s sufficient to know that _those_ campaigns match _that_ input id (which is actually a provider id on our end). So for us it’s enough to know that a provider is part of _those_ campaigns.

{quote}Are the menu item tags to figure out which items are excluded from the campaign? So if there was a price increase on an item excluded from the campaign, we should not remove that provider from the campaign.{quote}

Yes, exactly. We will not take this into consideration for the Milestone #1 (Admin Panel report), but the end goal is to be able to distinguish these, as well.

{quote}I think for menu item tags we have exclusion / inclusion separately.{quote}

Yes, let’s adjust the API specs to cover this, as well. Can you please adjust the API spec to cover this, as well? I see [there’s only one field in Admin Panel|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-campaign/eater/targetedCampaigns/edit/21730] with _Menu Item Tags_ and _Mode_ so probably this is the way we should represent it in the API, as well.

