Hi all\!

Adding here the legal memo we got from the law firm. There are some misunderstandings (ie Bolt Food is operated by Bolt Operations OÜ, not Bolt Services LT UAB), however, those do not affect the overall legal analysis.

*In conclusion remote selling of alcoholic beverages is not prohibited.* As selling in shops, selling remotely must comply with the requirements of the legislation. The main conditions are:
1) to provide true and comprehensive information on the beverages sold - therefore we should have similar disclaimer about the owner of the online store as on Wolt’s app;
2) to meet age restriction criteria (beverages must not be sold to anyone younger than 20 years of age and not sold by anyone younger than 18 years) - it is important that we have age verification in place, incl. the couriers obligation to check the ID; also the age restriction may be applied to couriers which means that the couriers need to be over 18 years old;
3) the alcohol may be sold (including delivery) only during the following hours: 10 a.m. and 8 p.m. on Mondays to Saturdays and between 10 a.m. and 3 p.m. on Sundays;
4) retailer shall issue documents for transporting alcoholic beverages to the address indicated by the customer - invoice should be issued by the retailer and sent to the client together with alochol.

[^Memo_Alcoholic beverages sales_220923_fin.docx]

Kind regards

Marilin

